  Let $\mathbf{X,Y}$ and $\mathbf{Z}$ be pairwise disjoint node sets in a $\mathrm{CPDAG}$ $(\mathrm{PAG})$ $\g$. If $\g$ is amenable relative to $(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y})$, then the following statements are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}[label = (\roman*)]
\item\label{l:eqa1} $\mathbf{Z}$ satisfies the forbidden set condition\xspace (see Definition~\ref{def:gac}) relative to $(\mathbf{X},\mathbf{Y})$ in~$\g$.
